From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 06:27:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: pmp-display: Name the PMP table checks
 after T8132

The J604 shares the PMP vote bridge with the J713, and the bridge checks
the PMP's apple,tunable-soc-device table with j713_disp_table() and
j713_agx_table(). The J604 passed these checks without any J604 data
behind them.

The live J604 device tree (25G83 stub, macOS 26B123) now provides that
data. Its table has the same shape, 34 records of 0x7c bytes. Record 12
(AGX) holds the identity words the AGX check expects, and record 15 is
DISP, as on the J713.

The checks are therefore not board-specific. Rename them t8132_*_table()
and say where the J604 data comes from. The checks themselves are
unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 217a84783bea876cc639179c1bc7091e4847c8b3)
---
 drivers/soc/apple/pmp-display.c | 15 +++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/pmp-display.c b/drivers/soc/apple/pmp-display.c
index 46c498e9f7..d30e677b02 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/pmp-display.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/pmp-display.c
@@ -171,7 +171,14 @@ static void pmp_vote_reply(struct pmp_power_vote *s, u8 endpoint, u64 word)
 	s->releasing = false;
 }
 
-static inline bool j713_disp_table(const void *data, size_t size)
+/*
+ * The retained PMP's apple,tunable-soc-device table: 34 records of 0x7c
+ * bytes, with DISP at record 15 and AGX at record 12. The checks are not
+ * J713-specific: the J604 live device tree (25G83 stub, macOS 26B123)
+ * carries the same 34 x 0x7c table, and its records 12 and 15 match the
+ * J713 in every field checked here.
+ */
+static inline bool t8132_disp_table(const void *data, size_t size)
 {
 	const u8 *p = data;
 
@@ -179,7 +186,7 @@ static inline bool j713_disp_table(const void *data, size_t size)
 		!memcmp(p + 15 * 0x7c + 0x74, "DISP\0\0\0\0", 8);
 }
 
-static inline bool j713_agx_table(const void *data, size_t size)
+static inline bool t8132_agx_table(const void *data, size_t size)
 {
 	const u8 *p = data;
 	unsigned int offset;
@@ -255,7 +262,7 @@ struct apple_pmp_display *apple_pmp_display_register(struct device *dev,
 	/* J713 and J604 share a qualified fixed table shape. */
 	table = of_get_property(dev->of_node, "apple,tunable-soc-device", &size);
 	if (!match || !of_property_present(dev->of_node, "apple,tunable-soc-device") ||
-	    !cookie || !send || (board && !j713_disp_table(table, size)))
+	    !cookie || !send || (board && !t8132_disp_table(table, size)))
 		return NULL;
 	mutex_lock(&pmp_display_registration);
 	if (pmp_display)
@@ -267,7 +274,7 @@ struct apple_pmp_display *apple_pmp_display_register(struct device *dev,
 	p->driver = dev->driver;
 	p->cookie = cookie;
 	p->send = send;
-	p->agx_table_valid = !board || j713_agx_table(table, size);
+	p->agx_table_valid = !board || t8132_agx_table(table, size);
 	mutex_init(&p->request);
 	spin_lock_init(&p->lock);
 	init_completion(&p->reply);
-- 
